# Windows launchers end their lines with CRLF in every checkout, ZIP and release: cmd.exe misreads
# blocks and labels of an LF-only .bat (the portable 0.0.2 shipped Start_GIMaP.bat with LF only).
# The two folder rules below come later and win for their own files.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
# The bundled 1D Predict model (Workflow V5) is checked file by file against SHA-256 manifests
# (conditional_v2/conditional_fast_manifest_v2.json and stable_blue_rc_v1/MANIFEST.json) before it
# runs. The checksums were taken from the bytes on disk, where some files end their lines with
# CRLF and others with LF, so git must hand out exactly those bytes on every computer:
# no line-ending conversion in this folder.
modules/Fitting_1D_Model/Workflow_v5/** -text
# The bundled Sputter toolkit (utils/sputter_toolkit) is checked file by file against its MANIFEST.json
# (sha256 of the bytes), and the network checkpoints are bound to the exact bytes of five of its source
# files. Its text files end their lines with LF; with core.autocrlf a checkout would turn them into CRLF:
# no line-ending conversion in this folder.
utils/sputter_toolkit/** -text
